# nr-relay-twin-web

## Cargo and workspace edits

None. The suite is JSON scenarios under native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/twin/scenarios/web/ read by the existing
`twin` target, and the ledger native/core/crates/mixdog-relay/tests/ledger/nr-relay-twin-web.json.
compose_flip.rs SERVICE_PENDING: no name is added or removed by this task.

## What the Rust relay must read for these scenarios

- The scenarios seed DATA_DIR/devices.json in the Node store layout (device id -> secretHash, clientTokenHash, clients
  {id -> tokenHash, name, platform, browser, createdAt, lastSeenAt}, optional appVersion / versionSeenAt): the Rust
  store must load it as the Node store does (the identity and crossover tasks need the same).
- Scenarios that use `files.mobile_release` only write valid records (an APK link or the releases-list link) or none.
